      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c075935d5cece4df39f010f|full_name}: I feel like its not for unoptimized avatars, but for avatars that could potentially harm someone in VR like when lots of flashing lights and camera warping screen-space shaders. Not everyone wants to block all shaders because a massive chunk of avatars will look gross or just bad without the intended shader. So a clear way to punish those who make troll avatars would be great. You can hit hide avatar, but if someone can be harmed by the flashing lights or disorienting camera they don't know that avatar does it until its too late and these avatars need to be reported.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
